Source: bdwn
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tom <tom@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: bdwn
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         restic,
         openssh-client,
         adduser
Suggests: zfsutils-linux
Description: Encrypted server backups to an SFTP repository
 BackDown (bdwn) backs up selected directories to a remote SFTP repository
 using restic. Backups are encrypted with a passphrase and driven by a
 systemd timer running as an unprivileged system user. Configuration lives
 in /etc/bdwn/bdwn.conf and the SSH connection in /var/lib/bdwn/.ssh/config.

Package: bdwn-libvirt
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         bdwn (>= ${source:Version}),
         libvirt-clients,
         qemu-utils
Description: Libvirt VM backups for BackDown
 Cold backups of libvirt virtual machines into the bdwn restic repository:
 clean shutdown, cold external snapshot, VM restart, then export of the
 stable base images and domain XML while the VM runs on the overlays.
 The overlays are then merged back, live when the host allows it, otherwise
 with the VM briefly stopped (qemu-img).
 A systemd timer template is provided, enable one instance per VM:
 systemctl enable --now bdwn-libvirt@<vm-name>.timer
